  message: "ADVANCED — non-governance portion MERGED (PR #651, 3b065bbf99): README (+ meta-package sync), docs/hypergumbo-spec.md, USE-CASES.md, CACHE.md, and concept-axes (via its generator scripts/generate-concept-axes) concept-renamed 'behavior map'->'survey'; stale 'hypergumbo run' / legacy-filename doc examples -> 'hypergumbo survey' / survey.json. The schema-stable view VALUE ('view':'behavior_map') and code symbols (load_behavior_map, the view field) are untouched. GOVERNANCE PORTION (needs approval): the .agent/ playbook sweep. SCOPE CORRECTION — this is SMALL, ~3 editable files, NOT the 215-file figure (that was inflated by never-edited tracker .ops op-logs + behavior_map CODE refs in hooks): (a) .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/self-analysis-dogfooding-playbook.md (2 concept refs + a 'hypergumbo run .' example), (b) .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/docstring-staleness-audit-playbook.md (1 concept ref: 'behavior map reports'), (c) 1 hook file with a 'behavior map' concept ref. Proposed change: rename the concept prose 'behavior map'->'survey' + the 'hypergumbo run' example -> 'hypergumbo survey' in those 3 files, keeping any behavior_map CODE/value refs. DEFERRED (low-value/ambiguous, non-governance): docs/example-output.md (captured/generated example — regenerates with the new concept) + docs/governance-case-critiques.md (point-in-time case study). Historical/migration docs keep vocabulary per ADR-0042 Neutral. Requesting human approval for the .agent/ 3-file governance change."  # 2cfc
